From b406c807c1a741121f6c452bb18824cc67886883 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timo <1788603+darknagel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:14:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] temp/libcamera: OnePlus 8 Pro camera tuning and statistics
 fixes

Colour correction matrices and lens shading tables for the main, ultrawide,
telephoto and front cameras, taken from the stock OnePlus tuning (cc13 and
lsc40 of com.qti.tuned.*.bin). The shading tables keep every gain at 1 or
above, so clipped highlights stay white, and are scaled so a flat field keeps
the colour and brightness the AWB and AGC measured before the correction; the
luminance targets are lowered by the same factor. The front camera leaves the
matrix out for now: with the grey world AWB it made mixed scenes yellow.

AGC: the default constraint (top 2 % at least 0.5) kept raising the gain
while the image clipped; replace it with a lower bound of 0.3 and an upper
bound of 0.7 for the 90-98 % quantiles.

Autofocus: coarse steps of 256 with fine steps of 64, longer warm-up and a
stricter stop, matching the new sharpness measure.

New libcamera patches:
0009 makes the sharpness measure robust against sensor noise (cored squared
differences, centre half of the frame, clipped pixels left out),
0010 calculates the statistics of the GPU debayer over the whole frame; they
covered only the top left corner of the image, which made the autofocus
focus on whatever was there and the AGC and AWB measure it.
